[size=4][b]A trash can and a sort button, in the inventory, where the mess is.[/b][/size]

[size=4][b]The can[/b][/size]

Pick an item up and click the can. It comes apart into what it was made of and the parts land in your bag.

The refund is not a number I invented. It is the item's own recipe - the same one the bench used to build it - paying the same amounts the bench charged, and skipping anything the game itself marks as not recoverable. One whole craft returns one whole craft's materials; a leftover that does not make a full craft returns nothing, the way the bench never sold you half a shield. Quality is paid for: a level 3 sword cost more than a level 1 and gives back more.

Anything with no recipe - wood, stone, ore, a handful of raspberries - has nothing to give back, so it is simply thrown away.

[size=4][b]The sort buttons[/b][/size]

One under the can for your own bag, one under Place Stacks for whatever chest is open.

Sorting groups by item type, then by name, then puts the best quality first. [b]It also pours split stacks back together[/b] - half a stack of wood here and half there come out as one pile, by the game's own stacking rule: same item, same quality, same world level.

Your hotbar row is never touched. Neither is anything living in an equipment or quick-slot row added by another mod - the boundary is read from Cartur's UI - HUD when it is installed, and from the inventory's own height when it is not.

[size=4][b]Worth knowing[/b][/size]

[b]The can destroys things.[/b] That is what it is for, and there is no undo. It asks no questions, exactly like dropping an item into lava, only tidier.

[b]No config file.[/b] Nothing in here needed a setting yet.

[size=4][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]

One postfix on InventoryGui.Show, which builds the buttons once and reuses them. No transpilers, no method replaced, nothing per frame. The Sort buttons are clones of the game's own Take All button, so they carry its skin, hover tint and click sound rather than art of mine. Client-side: nothing is synced, and the people you play with do not need it.

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]

Requires BepInEx. Unpack into your Valheim folder so the DLL lands in BepInEx/plugins.

